  "body": "## Overview\n\nAdds support for Tencent Hy-SimulMT, a simultaneous speech translation model (Hugging Face architecture `HYV3SpeechForCausalLM`, GGUF arch `hy_v3`, new projector type `hyv3_speech`)\n\nThe text architecture `hy_v3` is already supported. This PR adds the audio tower, in three parts:\n\n- **The audio tower** — a Whisper-style mel computed per segment, a conv2d + transformer encoder, and an FSK adapter that stacks encoder frames into LLM tokens.\n- **Turn-by-turn feeding** — the model was trained on 1600 ms of audio followed by 800 ms per turn, answering each turn before hearing the next one. `llama-mtmd-cli` detects this from the projector and feeds it that way automatically.\n- **Single-file GGUF support** — the published GGUFs carry the text model and the projector in one file, so there is no separate `mmproj`. `llama-mtmd-cli` falls back to `-m` when `--mmproj` is not given.\n\nThe models are published at <https://huggingface.co/tencent/Hy-SimulMT-30B-A3B-GGUF> (translation only) and <https://huggingface.co/tencent/Hy-SimulMT-30B-A3B-Interleave-GGUF> (source text and translation). The inference service, training tools and model card are at <https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-SimulMT>.\n\nChanges by area:\n\n| Area                  | File(s)                                                                              | Notes                                                                                     |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Audio encoder graph   | `tools/mtmd/models/hyv3-speech.cpp` (new)                                            | conv2d stack + sinusoidal pos + transformer + FSK adapter                                 |\n| Graph registration    | `tools/mtmd/models/models.h`, `tools/mtmd/CMakeLists.txt`                            | `clip_graph_hyv3_speech` + the two helpers for mel→token arithmetic                       |\n| Audio preprocessing   | `tools/mtmd/mtmd-audio.h`, `tools/mtmd/mtmd-audio.cpp`                               | `mtmd_audio_preprocessor_hyv3_speech`, cuts the mel on the training grid                  |\n| Projector plumbing    | `tools/mtmd/clip-impl.h`, `tools/mtmd/clip-model.h`, `tools/mtmd/clip.cpp`           | `PROJECTOR_TYPE_HYV3_SPEECH`, tensor names, hparams                                       |\n| mtmd wiring           | `tools/mtmd/mtmd.h`, `tools/mtmd/mtmd.cpp`                                           | preprocessor selection, audio markers, `mtmd_audio_stream_mode()`, `mtmd_has_projector()` |\n| Single-file projector | `src/llama-model-loader.cpp`, `tools/mtmd/mtmd-cli.cpp`                              | the leftover tensors belong to the projector, and `--mmproj` falls back to `-m`           |\n| Turn-by-turn feeding  | `tools/mtmd/mtmd-cli.cpp`                                                            | `run_turn_stream()` + dispatch on `MTMD_AUDIO_STREAM_TURN`                                |\n| GGUF constants        | `gguf-py/gguf/constants.py`                                                          | `VisionProjectorType.HYV3_SPEECH`                                                         |\n| Conversion            | `tools/mtmd/legacy-models/convert_hyv3_speech_mmproj.py` (new)                       | reads the `audio_tower.*` tensors out of the merged checkpoint                            |\n| Docs                  | `docs/multimodal/hyv3-speech.md` (new), `docs/multimodal.md`, `tools/mtmd/README.md` | guide + the two index links                                                               |\n\n## Additional information\n\n### Tensor naming\n\nThe tower reuses the existing `a.*` / `mm.*` names, so no new lookup path is needed. \n\n\n### Testing\n\nCPU-only build (`-DGGML_CUDA=OFF`), `Q4_K_M` single-file GGUF, 13.26 s sample:\n\n```\ndidn't do that他没有那样做，\n and then we have他然后我们有\n the additional problem他额外的问题，\n of the jury instruction他就是陪审团指示，\nrun_turn_stream: 87 tokens, 6/16 turns emitted, 13.26 s audio in 9.45 s (1.40x realtime)\n```\n\n(`他` is the target-branch marker, id 120809, printed to keep the two branches separable. A turn with no content is a WAIT, which is expected on most turns.) The translation matches the reference implementation.\n\n### Further Plan\n\n- **`llama-server`** does not run these GGUFs yet: it still expects the projector in a separate `--mmproj` file, and it does not feed audio turn by turn. Serving support is a follow-up; until then use `llama-mtmd-cli`.\n\n\n## Requirements\n\n- I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- AI usage disclosure: YES —\n",
